menu "Michi Music Stream Pairing"

    comment "Pairing window + controller registry (phase 10). The window opens ONLY from the physical button; tokens are stored as SHA-256 digests (never plaintext)."

    config MICHI_PAIRING_WINDOW_SECONDS
        int "Pairing window duration (s)"
        default 120
        range 10 3600
        help
          How long a pairing window (opened by the physical button)
          stays open before it expires and closes itself (one-shot
          esp_timer -> MICHI_EVENT_PAIRING_WINDOW_CLOSED, PAIRING -> IDLE
          in the FSM). A window also closes on a successful pairing or
          when the confirm-attempt limit is exhausted.

    config MICHI_PAIRING_MAX_CONTROLLERS
        int "Maximum paired controllers"
        default 8
        range 1 16
        help
          Maximum registry entries persisted in the NVS "michi_pairing"
          namespace (one versioned blob). Reaching the limit rejects new
          pairings until a controller is revoked.

    config MICHI_PAIRING_MAX_CHALLENGES_PER_WINDOW
        int "Max challenges per window"
        default 3
        range 1 10
        help
          Rate limit: how many challenges one window may issue. Each
          challenge request past the limit fails (ESP_ERR_TIMEOUT) until
          the window is re-opened by the button. Never 0: a window with
          no challenges could never be confirmed.

    config MICHI_PAIRING_MAX_CONFIRM_ATTEMPTS
        int "Max failed confirmations per window"
        default 5
        range 1 10
        help
          Anti brute force: every failed confirmation (wrong challenge,
          malformed credentials) consumes one attempt. When the limit is
          exceeded the window CLOSES (log + MICHI_EVENT_PAIRING_WINDOW_CLOSED)
          and can only be re-opened by the physical button.

endmenu
